d.1:3:
Returns the format for `mime_type`, or `None` if the type is unknown.

The aliases `image/jpg` and `image/tif` map to [`ImageFormat::Jpeg`] and [`ImageFormat::Tiff`].

```
use gpui::ImageFormat;

assert_eq!(ImageFormat::from_mime_type("image/jpg"), Some(ImageFormat::Jpeg));
assert_eq!(ImageFormat::Png.extension(), "png");
assert_eq!(ImageFormat::from_mime_type("text/plain"), None);
```

Returns the file extensions that `img` can decode, in lowercase and without the dot.

The list is the extensions of `image::ImageFormat` plus `svg`. gpui decides whether a file
loads by reading its bytes, not its extension, so the list is a guide.

# Examples

```
# use gpui::*;
assert!(Img::extensions().contains(&"png"));
assert!(Img::extensions().contains(&"svg"));
```

Runs `listener` when an action of type `A` is dispatched along the focus path, during the bubble phase.

Dispatch reaches this element when it is on the focus path. The listener receives the action and can
stop propagation or call [`App::propagate`]. This is the imperative equivalent of
[`InteractiveElement::on_action`].

# Example

```standalone_crate
use gpui::{actions, div, prelude::*, Context, Window};

actions!(counter_example, [Increment]);

struct Counter {
    count: usize,
}

impl Render for Counter {
    fn render(&mut self, _window: &mut Window, cx: &mut Context<Self>) -> impl IntoElement {
        div().on_action(cx.listener(|counter: &mut Counter, _: &Increment, _window, cx| {
            counter.count += 1;
            cx.notify();
        }))
    }
}
```
